# Iteration Generation Guide

This guide is for AI agents generating component iterations.

## Core Rules

### 1. Props Interface — NEVER Change

The iteration must be a drop-in replacement. Same props, same types.

```tsx
// ✅ Same props as original
export default function ArticleCard({ post, category, variant, className, onClick }: Props)

// ❌ Changed props — BREAKS the system
export default function ArticleCard({ post, category, layout, theme }: Props)
```

### 2. File Naming

```
{PascalCaseName}.iteration-{n}.tsx
```

Save it at **the exact path given in your prompt** (the prompt states the full `Save as …` path for every iteration). Do not assume the playground lives at `src/app/playground` — the host may mount it elsewhere.

`{PascalCaseName}` must match the **default export function name** (e.g. `ManifestoPage`, not `Manifesto`). This enables kebab-case conversion back to the registry ID.

### 3. Imports — REWRITE relative paths, never copy them verbatim

**This is the most common way an iteration breaks.** The iteration file is written to `<playground>/iterations/`, which is a **different directory than the original component**. Any relative (`../` or `./`) import copied from the original will silently re-anchor to the playground directory and fail to resolve.

Rewrite every relative import from the original into the host alias `@/`, which maps to the host's `src/`. Work out the original's real location from the `Source file` path given in your prompt, then convert.

```tsx
// Original: src/features/daily-recap/components/DailyRecapItem.tsx
import { calculateDailyMetrics } from "../hooks/useDailyRecap";
// ❌ copied verbatim into iterations/ → resolves to <playground>/hooks/useDailyRecap → BREAKS
// ✅ rewritten to the alias
import { calculateDailyMetrics } from "@/features/daily-recap/hooks/useDailyRecap";
```

Imports that are **already** aliased (`@/…`) or are bare packages (`react`, `lucide-react`) are copied unchanged — they resolve from anywhere. Only `../` and `./` imports need rewriting.

### 4. File Structure

```tsx
"use client";

// Bare packages: copy unchanged
import React from "react";
import { Calendar } from "lucide-react";
// Already aliased: copy unchanged
import { Separator } from "@/components/ui/separator";
// Was "../hooks/useDailyRecap" in the original → rewritten to the alias
import { calculateDailyMetrics } from "@/features/daily-recap/hooks/useDailyRecap";
// Type imports follow the same rule
import type { InsightPost } from "@/components/ArticleCard";

/**
 * @iteration 1
 * @parent ArticleCard
 * @description Horizontal card layout with image on left
 */

// Default export, SAME props interface
export default function ArticleCard({ post, category, variant = "expanded", className, onClick }: {
  post: InsightPost;
  // ... same as original
}) {
  // Your variation
}
```

### 5. Sequential Processing

Process iterations **one at a time**. For each:
1. Save the `.tsx` file
2. Update `iterations/tree.json` with the correct parent
3. Then proceed to the next

Do **not** edit `iterations/index.ts` — the server rebuilds it from written iteration files.

This gives the user immediate visual feedback as each iteration appears on the canvas.

### 6. Tailwind

Stick to existing Tailwind utilities and patterns. Don't introduce custom utilities or CSS-in-JS beyond what the source already uses. You may change colors, typography, spacing — just stay within the existing config.

## Layout Variation Ideas

| Change | Examples |
|--------|----------|
| Direction | Row ↔ Column, LTR ↔ RTL |
| Grid | 1-col → 2-col, card grid → list |
| Ordering | Image first → text first |
| Grouping | Flat → nested sections |
| Responsive | Stack on mobile, side-by-side on desktop |

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Props interface unchanged
- [ ] No relative (`../` / `./`) imports copied from the original — all rewritten to `@/`
- [ ] All imports resolve
- [ ] Metadata comment included
- [ ] File named correctly (`{PascalCase}.iteration-{n}.tsx`)
- [ ] Default export with same function name
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] `tree.json` updated with correct parent
- [ ] Each iteration is meaningfully distinct
